{"title":"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An acute-angled triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has orthocentre <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. The circle passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> with centre the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />. Similarly, the circle passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> with centre the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> intersects the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243af6fad28c15abb3e11996374ba60e745bf543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/368b6f971b418d731c62ff2cb59f51c527d22849.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, and the circle passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> with centre the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersects the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />. Show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a8ae66ded7f33f9385a37c9cadfb82720013d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243af6fad28c15abb3e11996374ba60e745bf543.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/8/368b6f971b418d731c62ff2cb59f51c527d22849.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> lie on a circle.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:IMO20081.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/5/53/IMO20081.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"465\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/0429f4c41dcb7a6dbe033b6c4ae5aac177481024.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/5846471a9c6932ed651aded7c6fcc0a81d611846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d614d1d2865e804ec88528dad52d43ad04d3654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" /> be the midpoints of sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. It's not hard to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/d/a3d8310207514d806cf15dcfa626c01a3eaeae72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_BM_C\\parallel BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />. We also have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/219b69450beb7b387f42645b4429d631551a32d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH\\perp BC$\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7c2f17d6be9659ddceb221ec8c74e2406ef3a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH \\perp M_BM_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"15\" />. Now note that the radical axis of two circles is perpendicular to the line connecting their centers. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is on the radical axis of the circles centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/5846471a9c6932ed651aded7c6fcc0a81d611846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d614d1d2865e804ec88528dad52d43ad04d3654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is too. We then have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/c/a4ca38821773bcb234491002ae6be049b2b2baba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC_1\\cdot AC_2=AB_2\\cdot AB_1\\Rightarrow \\frac{AB_2}{AC_1}=\\frac{AC_2}{AB_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"320\" height=\"42\" />. This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f782382a256cc4cba501d0eaa076d617d822265e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AB_2C_1\\sim \\triangle AC_2B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"165\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a7d4500d7bbf48a61dfab229f1f14c8114ec74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AB_2C_1=\\angle AC_2B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"159\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b00b4fc98efff5572119a1976c0a33f26d0ff17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle C_1B_2B_1=180^{\\circ}-\\angle AB_2C_1=180^{\\circ}-\\angle AC_2B_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"373\" height=\"15\" />. This shows that quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc3024ad59242d1a594571454c6501f938d392d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1C_2B_1B_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> is cyclic. Note that the center of its circumcircle is at the intersection of the perpendicular bisectors of the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/768d476e47994f734c8e8d991f020d78853f3336.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f98f18b30f6c249ca5b2f65ae693caa835e576ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B_1B_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />. However, these are just the perpendicular bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, which meet at the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, so the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/3/dc3024ad59242d1a594571454c6501f938d392d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1C_2B_1B_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> is the circumcenter of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Similarly, the circumcenters of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fd7ea407497d42a9815678db0ae96fde335457a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1A_2B_1B_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/e/3aea189613ec689475f511198fb44594d0e0a673.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1C_2A_1A_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> are coincident with the circumcenter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. The desired result follows.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO\" title=\"2008 IMO\">2008 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017065109\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 288/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 866/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 51/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8945/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.930      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.930      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9772:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017065109 and revision id 204528. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}